{
  "_note": "Skill map for competency 12, OpenBIM & Interoperability. Each skill is broken into the specific things a learner must know or be able to do (components) behind its Acceptance Criteria. Existing lessons are placed on the map, never changed. Planned lessons are written one component at a time, then 'mix' lessons combine components and 'reinforce' lessons bring them back later. Reviewed by: (pending Kirk + Alex Hanna). Drafted 2026-09-21.",
  "competency_id": 12,
  "competency": "OpenBIM & Interoperability",
  "roles": {
    "teach": "introduces one component",
    "practise": "the learner applies one component in a scenario",
    "mix": "two or more components together, closer to the real task",
    "reinforce": "short retrieval of earlier components after a gap"
  },
  "skills": [
    {
      "skill_id": "SKL-114",
      "level": 1,
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Name IFC, BCF, IDS, bSDD and COBie and say what each carries (model, issues, requirements, definitions, handover data)",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "openbim-standards-overview",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "Given a job to do on a project, pick the standard that does it",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "planned": "openbim-standards-pick",
              "role": "practise"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "Explain how the five fit together in one exchange (IDS says what, IFC carries it, BCF reports problems, bSDD defines terms, COBie hands over)",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "planned": "openbim-standards-one-exchange",
              "role": "mix"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill_id": "SKL-23",
      "level": 1,
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Say what openBIM is and what vendor-neutral means",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "vendor-neutral-data",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "Name the downstream risks of proprietary-only data: reopening in 10 years, changing tools, supply-chain members on other software, owner access after handover",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "vendor-neutral-data",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "Spot lock-in in a real situation (a deliverable, an archive, a contract clause) and say what open alternative fixes it",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "planned": "vendor-lock-in-spot-it",
              "role": "practise"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill_id": "SKL-24",
      "level": 2,
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Say what an MVD is: a subset of IFC for one exchange purpose, not a quality level",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "ifc-export-mvds",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "Match the MVD to what the recipient will do with the file (reference / transfer / handover)",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "ifc-export-mvds-apply",
              "role": "practise",
              "status": "draft"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "Read the BEP exchange table for the IFC version and MVD each drop requires, and raise it when the MVD is missing",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "ifc-export-read-the-bep",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "draft"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "d",
          "text": "Set the export so property sets, classification and coordinates survive. Hands off to SKL-11 (Model Federation & Validation), whose acceptance criteria is exactly this.",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "ifc-export-settings-that-matter",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "draft",
              "note": "tagged SKL-11 component b after the blind alignment check picked SKL-11"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "e",
          "text": "Check the exported file contains what the recipient needs before issuing (hands off to SKL-116)",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "planned": "ifc-export-end-to-end",
              "role": "mix",
              "note": "uses c + d + SKL-116"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill_id": "SKL-116",
      "level": 2,
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Explain why the authoring tool cannot be trusted to show what the export contains",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "checking-ifc-in-neutral-viewers",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "b",
          "text": "Run the pre-issue check: geometry present, placement, sample elements' properties, classification, units",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "slug": "checking-ifc-in-neutral-viewers",
              "role": "teach",
              "status": "published"
            },
            {
              "planned": "neutral-viewer-check-drill",
              "role": "practise"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "c",
          "text": "Diagnose the common failures a viewer reveals (missing psets, wrong origin, elements exported as proxies) back to the export setting that caused them",
          "lessons": [
            {
              "planned": "neutral-viewer-diagnose",
              "role": "practise"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "skill_id": "SKL-115",
      "level": 2,
      "components": [
        {
          "id": "a",
          "text": "Link rather than convert, and say why",
